   "raisedBy": "Review feedback",
   "was": "The Nike Community Store on NE Martin Luther King Jr. Blvd was Portland's recommended debut door for every Portland-specific drop. Six opportunities, five calendar entries, the retail playbook, the uniform plan and four dossiers sent launches there.",
   "now": "The store (2650 NE MLK Jr. Blvd, open since 1984) closed in late 2022 after theft and safety concerns, and Nike confirmed in September 2023 that it won't reopen. It is removed as a door everywhere. Albina launches now go to Albina partner venues. Downtown Nike Portland (638 SW 5th Ave, reopened Nov 13, 2025, running on its main floor) is named only with the condition that it agrees to carry Blazers product, which is unconfirmed.",
   "why": "The fact-check marked the store 'unverifiable' from model knowledge and the brief kept it as its main launch door. Knowledge-mode research can't see closures.",
   "evidence": "OPB and KPTV (both Sept 8, 2023) report Nike's statement that the NE Portland store will not reopen. KOIN later reported the building would become a gym. Nike's newsroom and Willamette Week (Nov 12, 2025) report the downtown store reopening Nov 13, 2025.",
