   "found": "2026-10-10",
   "raisedBy": "Review feedback",
   "was": "The Knicks brief said the last ring came on May 10, 1973 'at the Garden', and the culture dossier said 'Game 5 at the Garden'.",
   "now": "The Knicks clinched the 1973 title with a 102-93 Game 5 win at the Forum in Inglewood on May 10, 1973, taking the series 4-1. The 1970 title, not 1973, was won at the Garden. Corrected in the brief, the culture dossier and the fact-check.",
   "why": "The original culture dossier had it right. The knowledge-mode fact-checker 'corrected' it to the Garden from model knowledge, and the brief then repeated the error.",
   "evidence": "Wikipedia's 1973 NBA Finals entry, ESPN's 2026 retrospective and NBA.com's Game 5 video all place the clincher at the Forum. MSG Network's restored tape is described as the May 10, 1973 game played at The Forum.",
